what: the certificate chain that Android's emulator gave Datapavan's hardware check, captured on the maintainer's
  computer with the debug build's lab record (ADR 0040; adb logcat -s DatapavanAttestationLab,
  scripts/attestation-chain-from-logcat.py), with the emulator booted read-only from these SDK images. The
  debug build was signed with a throwaway debug key, made only for these captures (its certificate's SHA-256
  begins dc0043e7b001dc98), so that no developer's own debug key is in the leaves.
sdk35.pem: system-images;android-35;google_apis;x86_64, revision 9 (userdebug, security patch 2024-09-05), AVD
  dp-api35-ci (the CI image); the check said: verdict TEST_ROOT, level 0 (software), 3 certificates. Its
  KeyMint is AOSP's in-process C++ service (android.hardware.security.keymint-service, KeyMint 300), whose
  attestation key came from Google's Remote Key Provisioning service for unregistered devices: intermediate
  "O=TEE, CN=977cc1f929de582ef099b0e57d4c900d", valid 2026-11-05 to 2026-11-21, under the root
  "CN=Droid Unregistered Device CA, O=Google Test LLC", self-signed, valid 2026-11-05 to 2027-01-16,
  SubjectPublicKeyInfo SHA-256 51894c6169633e9f928538774e91838a50dcc27cf02dd3f420bb0c018492c679. The
  intermediate lives about two weeks, so tests judge this chain at fixed dates.
sdk30.pem: system-images;android-30;google_apis;x86_64, revision 16 (userdebug, security patch 2021-08-05),
  AVD dp-api30; the check said: verdict SOFTWARE_ROOT, level 0, 3 certificates. Its keystore is Keymaster 4.1
  in software (attestation version 4, keymaster version 41), signing under AOSP's software attestation
  intermediate (serial 1001, expired 2026-01-08) and root (SubjectPublicKeyInfo SHA-256
  d5100c7942ef2e8310dc30ef82729680cf48d690735c3f68179a33c7c370f286), whose private keys AOSP publishes
  (system/keymaster, contexts/soft_attestation_cert.cpp).
leaves: each leaf names the app that asked (org.visadahyu.datapavan, version 3) and the SHA-256 of the
  throwaway key's certificate that signed the build, and carries a random challenge; nothing else of the
  computer or its owner.
licence: certificates are facts issued by AOSP's software keymaster (Apache-2.0) and by Google's provisioning
  service; the capture is the project's, CC0-1.0.
